READ: high unif_r2 (near 1) = the attenuation is close to a single
      uniform scale c across traits -> c cancels in cov2cor(), so
      corr_mae should be small even though trace_mean is far from 1.
      Low unif_r2 = trait-dependent attenuation -> correlations distorted,
      and corr_mae should track that (not be small just because trace is off).

